  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ringgit Ledger",
    "overview": "Duitful looks like a household ledger kept on warm paper. The page is a cream stock, the writing is near-black ink, and the cards are slightly whiter sheets laid on top. Almost nothing is coloured. That restraint has a purpose: the user is reading their own money, often with some worry, and a calm page lets the few coloured marks mean something.\n\nThe colour that does appear is borrowed from the Malaysian banknote series. A blue mark is an RM 1 sized amount, green RM 5, red RM 10, orange RM 20, teal RM 50, purple RM 100 and above. Every user already reads that scale without a legend, so it carries the size of a number at a glance. Terracotta, the colour of the wallet logo, marks where you are and what has focus. Red is reserved for trouble.\n\nDensity is a phone ledger: one column of cards, rows separated by hairlines, figures right-aligned in tabular digits. On wider screens the same cards flow into columns and navigation moves to the side; the cards themselves do not change.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper surfaces in three steps (stage, background, card), in light and in dark.",
      "Ink for text and for every action. No coloured buttons.",
      "Banknote hues carry amount size and nothing else.",
      "Terracotta for identity, location and focus only.",
      "Red only when something is actually wrong.",
      "One serif moment per screen: the wordmark and the balance.",
      "Flat cards with hairline borders; shadows are reserved for things that float."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Banknote Rule",
        "body": "Chroma states the size of a number. If a colour is not telling the user how big an amount is, where they are, or that something is wrong, it should be ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Trouble Rule",
        "body": "Red means trouble. Having a debt is not an error, so debt totals and upcoming payments are plain ink. Overdue, overspent and negative are red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token Tint Rule",
        "body": "Soft washes are written as `color-mix(in srgb, var(--token) N%, transparent)`, never as a literal `rgba()` of the light value. A literal navy tint disappears on a dark card.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scarce Serif Rule",
        "body": "Fraunces is for the wordmark and the one headline figure. Card titles are Inter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine Text Rule",
        "body": "Monospace is for text a machine produced or will read. Words like \"Min payment\" or \"Instalment\" are Inter, even inside a badge.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Sheet Rule",
        "body": "If it scrolls with the page it has no drop shadow. Shadows mean \"this is floating above your ledger\": dialogs, menus, toasts.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Blur Rule",
        "body": "The only frosted surface is the bottom tab bar (88% stage colour, 14px blur), because content scrolls underneath it. The `--glass-*` tokens are historical names for solid card colours and do not blur.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Radii Rule",
        "body": "Use `--r-xs`, `--r-sm`, `--r-md` or `--r-pill`. A literal pixel radius is a bug.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read every colour from a token in `:root`, and keep the two dark blocks in `styles.css` identical to each other.",
      "**Do** write tints as `color-mix()` of a token so they survive the theme switch.",
      "**Do** use ink for actions. The primary button is `text` on light and warm sand on dark.",
      "**Do** set amounts in Inter 500 with tabular digits, right-aligned.",
      "**Do** keep body and caption text at 4.5:1 or better; `ink2` and `muted` are tuned for that on a card.",
      "**Do** keep touch targets at 44px or more.",
      "**Do** respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; give every new animation a reduced variant, as the existing ones have."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use a banknote hue, terracotta or red for decoration. Each has one meaning.",
      "**Don't** colour a debt total or a normal upcoming payment red.",
      "**Don't** add a radius outside the four, or a drop shadow to anything that scrolls with the page.",
      "**Don't** set words in monospace, or a second heading in Fraunces.",
      "**Don't** hard-code a hex or `rgba()` in a component rule, or reference a token that `:root` does not define.",
      "**Don't** add blur or glass to cards; only the bottom bar is frosted.",
      "**Don't** put a card inside a card."
    ]
  }
}